{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt","id":456324,"title":"What can exalt?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-24T16:20:48-07:00","id":456324,"title":"What can exalt?","content":"I was thinking about Exalted and the potential for crossovers with other settings (read: Nox did it), and I had a thought, what can actual exalt?<br /> The purpose of this thread is to discuss beings that people think could and couldn't Exalt from other settings, I'll start:<br /> Can't Exalt:<br /> The Avatar - Avatar, the Last Airbender and Legend of Korra - I do think benders can exalt, but would find it harder than regular mortals, the avatar her/himself could not exalt due to their soul being bound to Raava.<br /> <br /> Planeswalkers - Magic the Gathering - Once again, their soul structure. The planeswalker sparks would probably interfere with any exaltation process.<br /> <br /> Changelings, Prometheans, Vampires, Sin-eaters, etc. - World of Darkness - Don't know to much about how the souls of the World of Darkness splats works, but those are the ones I'm sure would have souls to messed up, or simply lacking souls, to Exalt. I suspect mages could as not exalt, and possibly werewolves, but I don't know how they get their powers<br /> <br /> Can Exalt:<br /> Tenno - Warframe - No soul modification, that we know of, but probably treated like wyld mutants, losing their capability for using warframes.<br /> <br /> Sparks - Girl Genius - Once again, no known soul modification, but would really have to prove their abilities.<br /> <br /> Wizards - Harry Potter - No reason not for them to exalt. Except maybe Voldemort with all the ripping of his own soul to make his horcruxes<br /> <br /> Sorcerers - Skulduggery Pleasant - Same as the wizards, except the Skulduggery 'cus he is a skeleton.<br /> <br /> Shur'tugal (dragon riders) - Inheritance Cycle - No mention of modification to their souls, but the bond with the dragon might affect their chances.<br /> <br /> Novas - Aberrant - Could exalt, but their mutation that gives them their powers might be treated as a wyld mutatation, causing a lose of powers.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ __________<br /> That's not a finite list that we can talk about on this thread, but it's all I can think of at this hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T16:31:06-07:00","id":456354,"title":"","content":"Living humans can Exalt.<br /> <br /> Some of the things you mention could be very specific kinds of Exalts - the Avatar makes me think of an Exigent, for example.<br /> <br /> Sparks are already basically more-aware Autochthonian demiurges and Twilights in theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:19:53-07:00","id":456377,"title":"","content":"As with a lot of crossovers, it really kinda boils down to interpretation and personal ruling, probably best handled on a case-by-case basis. I personally wouldn't root it as literally in having a human soul as the predominant litmus test. Not least because if going that far, one should likely also factor in that the dual-soul structure of Creation's mortals is not exactly the most common setting assumption. By default, this would rule out any setting in which the soul is ever demonstrated to be otherwise. And, since the topic is almost never broached, you'd have to make the big assumption that a setting in question has mortal souls structured like those of Creation.<br /> <br /> Then, as Zelbinnean notes, some things in other settings functionally already are Exalted. &quot;Sparks are basically Twilights,&quot; &quot;The Avatar is basically an Exigent,&quot; &quot;Batman is <s>the night</s> basically a Night,&quot; are all incredibly reasonable takes. Lots of details are different, obviously, but it'd be a weird thing to Exalt any such individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:30:41-07:00","id":456384,"title":"","content":"I swear I once read that animals could Exalt.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.savethechildren.org/atf/cf/%7B9def2ebe-10ae-432c-9bd0-df91d2eba74a%7D/LASSIE.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:32:32-07:00","id":456385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456384#post456384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear I once read that animals could Exalt.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.savethechildren.org/atf/cf/%7B9def2ebe-10ae-432c-9bd0-df91d2eba74a%7D/LASSIE.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be... the Shard version of Lunars me thinks? Or the reference from &quot;Games of Divinity&quot; about Gaian Exalts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:32:44-07:00","id":456386,"title":"","content":"basically anything that can be called human, human+ works but generally you will burn off almost all the advantages/disadvantages of whatever the extra is when the exaltation takes over unless you are spending points to keep it. only if it is obviously not human should not be able to exalt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:50:15-07:00","id":456395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456384#post456384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear I once read that animals could Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure it was an 'end of the world' scenario, where all of humanity was destroyed, but Creation is still there. Unable to bond to humans, exaltation no longer exist. Except for Lunars...being a last ditch attempt, Lunar Exaltation begins bonding to animals, and giving them a &quot;human&quot; true form.<br /> <br /> These Lunars could then breed new humans, which would almost instantly be exalted by one of the other types. So the Lunars could be a very last resort to saving Humanity.<br /> <br /> But I can't remember where I heard it. Maybe in some Ink Monkey notes? Or one of the writers/devs mentioning it...bah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:52:29-07:00","id":456396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456385#post456385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be... the Shard version of Lunars me thinks? Or the reference from &quot;Games of Divinity&quot; about Gaian Exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an emergency failsafe mentioned in the back of the Lunars book that took advantage of the loophole that whilst <i>one</i> of a lunars true forms had to be human it didn't technically need to be the one they were born in. I think the current consensus is that it either doesn't exist or is at least sealed until such time as it becomes a necessity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:03:37-07:00","id":456403,"title":"","content":"I think this was some first edition thing. Something about truly superb examples of an animal species getting a Solar Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:17:50-07:00","id":456446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456403#post456403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this was some first edition thing. Something about truly superb examples of an animal species getting a Solar Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read all the 1e stuff so it's possible I missed something, but you may be thinking of Animal Avatars as referred to in the Book of Three Circles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of Three Circles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as Solar Exalted are the lords of humanity, Gaia granted great powers to a handful of animals of every type and charged these magical beasts with the task of protecting and ruling their own kind.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of Three Circles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal avatars recognize that Solar Exalted are beings of equal stature.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth mentioning that the Book of Three Circles was made non-canon later in 1e with the release of Savant and Sorcerer. Avatar Animals and Totem Animals did come up later, but not quite in the same form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-24-2015, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:19:14-07:00","id":456452,"title":"","content":"I personally like the idea of animals Exalting as Lunars with a human true form, but I understand if people are iffy about it. Exaltations are supposed to be human things.<br /> <br /> I've never heard anyone mention animals Exalting as anything but Lunars though. Then again, I've not read 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:32:23-07:00","id":456464,"title":"","content":"It hails from the Storyteller section of the Lunars Manual as an interesting possibility that tables could go after, not strictly something canon. Errata Team Prime evidently felt strongly enough that it not be true to include a little, &quot;Can animals Exalt as Lunars? No,&quot; bit in the Scroll of Errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:38:03-07:00","id":456469,"title":"","content":"That's good to know. I appreciate the information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:38:34-07:00","id":456470,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd like to see different flavours of Exaltation that can affect beings other than humans, like Gaian Exalts for animals and ghostly champions Chosen by the Twin Monarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:40:03-07:00","id":456473,"title":"","content":"Anything you can call &quot;human&quot; with a straight face is a viable candidate, IMO. Warhammer 40k Space Marines? Probably not. Wizards in the Dresdenverse? Sure. White Court Vampires from the same? Nuh uh.<br /> <br /> I do agree that some types of beings, like Sparks and the Avatar are functionally Exalted already, though, so no double dipping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T19:28:25-07:00","id":456493,"title":"","content":"I don't know, a Solar Space Marine sounds suitably crazy awesome enough to me that I'd allow it. Honestly I would be rather easy going about what I'd allow to exalt personally. The deciding factor would come down to what fits the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T19:32:55-07:00","id":456495,"title":"","content":"First Edition Animal Avatars were pretty much just animals with Zenith charms, if I recall correctly. Pretty sure it was less of a &quot;these animals are Solar Exalts&quot; and more of a &quot;easy way to represent their abilities mechanically using existing rules&quot; thing, though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T01:20:55-07:00","id":456643,"title":"","content":"In a crossover scenario, I think you gotta examine what that fictional world uses as its narrative equivalent to what Exaltation represents as a meta-concept. Superman definitely isn't going to Exalt as a Zenith Caste, because his Kryptonian powers essentially are Exaltation. On the other hand, I think Mr. Spock could probably Exalt\u2014the setting's broad construction of &quot;human&quot; can probably accommodate what are basically pointy-eared humans from a different branch of a forerunner race's panspermia project. Katara's not gonna Exalt. Jace won't. Chuubo won't. It's a feel sort of thing, and should definitely err in favor of accommodating the crossover as a viable concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T01:59:49-07:00","id":456659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456643#post456643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I think Mr. Spock could probably Exalt\u2014the setting's broad construction of &quot;human&quot; can probably accommodate what are basically pointy-eared humans from a different branch of a forerunner race's panspermia project.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saddened, Mr. Vance. Spock is half-human, and we already know half-humans can Exalt, so it was already obvious that Spock could Exalt. Your argument actually proves that <i>Sarek</i> can Exalt.<br /> <br /> Of course, even assuming Sarek can Exalt, there are other questions. <br /> <br /> For example, can Trill Exalt? What about Trill symbionts? If the symbionts can't be Exalted directly, what happens when a joined Trill Exalts, and then later the host dies, but the symbiont is saved? What happens if an unjoined Trill Exalts, and then is joined to a symbiont from a Joined Trill that Exalted and then later died? What if the unjoined Exalted Trill was the child of Jadzia Dax and Worf (secretly rescued by Dr. Bashir after she died), creating a Exalted Klingon/Trill joined to a symbiont from a Exalted-while-joined Trill? WHAT THEN?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T02:29:34-07:00","id":456669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456659#post456659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am saddened, Mr. Vance. Spock is half-human, and we already know half-humans can Exalt, so it was already obvious that Spock could Exalt. Your argument actually proves that <i>Sarek</i> can Exalt.<br /> <br /> Of course, even assuming Sarek can Exalt, there are other questions.<br /> <br /> For example, can Trill Exalt? What about Trill symbionts? If the symbionts can't be Exalted directly, what happens when a joined Trill Exalts, and then later the host dies, but the symbiont is saved? What happens if an unjoined Trill Exalts, and then is joined to a symbiont from a Joined Trill that Exalted and then later died? What if the unjoined Exalted Trill was the child of Jadzia Dax and Worf (secretly rescued by Dr. Bashir after she died), creating a Exalted Klingon/Trill joined to a symbiont from a Exalted-while-joined Trill? WHAT THEN?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really saw much for the Trill symbionts in DS9 to call them the kind of things I could see as earning an exaltation, so I would say no to an exalted symbiont at my table. An unbonded Trill exalting would be the same as a normal person exalting. If a Trill was joined and then exalted I would again see it as the full person exalting, but since I've never seen indication that the symbionts are even sentient I would say the exaltation grafts onto the humanoid soul and when that person dies the exaltation moves on. A symbiont who had been joined to an exalt is only going to allow a memory and skill boost like the joining normally does. So I mean it comes down to the exalt would get more memories to deal with. The Trill were a rather dull species IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T03:52:35-07:00","id":456689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456659#post456659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, can Trill Exalt? What about Trill symbionts? If the symbionts can't be Exalted directly, what happens when a joined Trill Exalts, and then later the host dies, but the symbiont is saved? What happens if an unjoined Trill Exalts, and then is joined to a symbiont from a Joined Trill that Exalted and then later died? What if the unjoined Exalted Trill was the child of Jadzia Dax and Worf (secretly rescued by Dr. Bashir after she died), creating a Exalted Klingon/Trill joined to a symbiont from a Exalted-while-joined Trill? WHAT THEN?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just getting ready to go to bed, but now I think I will lay here in bed for the next 5 hours, unable to sleep because I can't stop thinking about this. Thanks for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T05:22:36-07:00","id":456752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456659#post456659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, can Trill Exalt? What about Trill symbionts? If the symbionts can't be Exalted directly, what happens when a joined Trill Exalts, and then later the host dies, but the symbiont is saved? What happens if an unjoined Trill Exalts, and then is joined to a symbiont from a Joined Trill that Exalted and then later died? What if the unjoined Exalted Trill was the child of Jadzia Dax and Worf (secretly rescued by Dr. Bashir after she died), creating a Exalted Klingon/Trill joined to a symbiont from a Exalted-while-joined Trill? WHAT THEN?</div> </div> </div> </div>At first, it looks like an easy question; the Trill exalts, while the joined symbiont is unaffected (beside the fact it is not joined to an Exalt). But... What happens if the joined Trill exalts as a Lunar and then change shape?!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T07:46:07-07:00","id":456844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456752#post456752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first, it looks like an easy question; the Trill exalts, while the joined symbiont is unaffected (beside the fact it is not joined to an Exalt). But... What happens if the joined Trill exalts as a Lunar and then change shape?!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing that happens if a regular Lunar gets pregnant (or gets a tapeworm). Shapeshifting doesn't harm the baby, ergo it doesn't harm the symbiont. Problem solved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:53:21-07:00","id":457578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456446#post456446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth mentioning that the Book of Three Circles was made non-canon later in 1e with the release of Savant and Sorcerer. Avatar Animals and Totem Animals did come up later, but not quite in the same form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they go back to something resembling their original form.<br /> In their current incarnation they're the god of their species and I think it's more interesting to have the god and the Animal Avatar as seperate entities. With the Animal Avatar directly representing the species and the god who, while having a vested interest in preventing the species from going extinct also potentially expands their purview based on the animals significance to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T06:02:54-07:00","id":1521325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/456324-what-can-exalt?p=456395#post456395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure it was an 'end of the world' scenario, where all of humanity was destroyed, but Creation is still there. Unable to bond to humans, exaltation no longer exist. Except for Lunars...being a last ditch attempt, Lunar Exaltation begins bonding to animals, and giving them a &quot;human&quot; true form.<br /> <br /> These Lunars could then breed new humans, which would almost instantly be exalted by one of the other types. So the Lunars could be a very last resort to saving Humanity.<br /> <br /> But I can't remember where I heard it. Maybe in some Ink Monkey notes? Or one of the writers/devs mentioning it...bah.</div> </div> </div> </div>building off of this you could even have the lunar exaltations exalt animals that have a lunar ancestor and technically because of that on some level they still kinda count as human, if you want to go even farther with the idea you could say that most animals would have a lunar ancestor somewhere just because if you go far enough back you'll find all kinds of crazy things in your ancestry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}